1
00:00:01,790 --> 00:00:06,350
Hello, I'm Dr. Sonia
Rivera-Martinez, Associate

2
00:00:06,350 --> 00:00:08,990
Professor, Department
of Family Medicine,

3
00:00:08,990 --> 00:00:13,280
and today I will be discussing
clinical dyslipidemia.

4
00:00:15,710 --> 00:00:19,170
Our session objectives
are as follows.

5
00:00:19,570 --> 00:00:22,130
We will describe the
main features for the

6
00:00:22,130 --> 00:00:24,810
different types of
lipopropine disorders,

7
00:00:24,890 --> 00:00:28,930
and then explain their
role in disease. 1.

8
00:00:29,110 --> 00:00:32,170
Identify the main features for

9
00:00:32,170 --> 00:00:34,970
primary causes of dyslipidemia.

10
00:00:34,970 --> 00:00:38,190
2. Examine the
main features for

11
00:00:38,190 --> 00:00:41,610
secondary causes
of dyslipidemia.

12
00:00:41,930 --> 00:00:44,330
Then we will correlate
the presenting

13
00:00:44,330 --> 00:00:46,430
signs and symptoms
with the different

14
00:00:46,430 --> 00:00:48,990
types of dyslipidemia
disorders.

15
00:00:49,150 --> 00:00:52,470
And lastly, we will
explain the rationale

16
00:00:52,470 --> 00:00:55,810
for the different
preventative strategies for

17
00:00:55,810 --> 00:01:00,830
dyslipidemia disorders
and formulate a

18
00:01:00,830 --> 00:01:03,710
treatment plan based on
the latest guidelines.

19
00:01:05,010 --> 00:01:07,910
We will now proceed
with the definition

20
00:01:07,910 --> 00:01:11,050
and classification
of dyslipidemia.

21
00:01:11,890 --> 00:01:16,410
Disorders of lipoprotein
metabolism can be primary,

22
00:01:16,410 --> 00:01:21,150
caused by genetic conditions,
or secondary to other

23
00:01:21,150 --> 00:01:25,350
medical conditions or
environmental exposure and involve

24
00:01:25,350 --> 00:01:30,650
either of substantial increase
or decrease in specific

25
00:01:30,650 --> 00:01:35,230
circulating lipids or
lipoproteins. Lipoprotein

26
00:01:35,230 --> 00:01:40,310
disorders can have a number
of clinical consequences.

27
00:01:41,530 --> 00:01:45,590
Lipoproteins are
complexes of lipids and

28
00:01:45,590 --> 00:01:49,010
proteins. They are
essential for transport of

29
00:01:49,010 --> 00:01:52,870
cholesterol, triglycerides,
and fat-soluble vitamins

30
00:01:52,870 --> 00:01:56,230
in the blood. They
also play essential

31
00:01:56,230 --> 00:02:01,010
roles in the absorption
of dietary cholesterol,

32
00:02:01,190 --> 00:02:05,730
long-chain fatty acids,
and fat-soluble vitamins.

33
00:02:08,350 --> 00:02:13,010
There are several
classes of lipoproteins

34
00:02:13,010 --> 00:02:15,570
which are classified primarily

35
00:02:15,570 --> 00:02:19,310
by their lipid
content per particle.

36
00:02:20,550 --> 00:02:23,270
Chylomicrons, they are
considered to be the

37
00:02:23,270 --> 00:02:27,090
least dense lipoprotein,
meaning that they are

38
00:02:27,090 --> 00:02:31,790
the most lipid rich.
On the other hand, high

39
00:02:31,790 --> 00:02:37,110
-density lipoprotein has
the least lipid content.

40
00:02:38,690 --> 00:02:44,610
This image demonstrates the
relationship of lipoproteins

41
00:02:44,610 --> 00:02:50,490
by density and size, which
are inversely related.

42
00:02:50,840 --> 00:02:54,660
You can see that the
HDL is the smallest

43
00:02:55,520 --> 00:02:58,530
lipoprotein, but yet
it's high in density,

44
00:02:58,530 --> 00:03:02,490
contrary to the
chylomicron, which is the

45
00:03:02,490 --> 00:03:05,990
largest in size but
has the least density.

46
00:03:10,180 --> 00:03:13,870
Lipoproteins are involved
in the transport of lipids.

47
00:03:13,970 --> 00:03:18,170
Chylomicrons, they
transport dietary lipids

48
00:03:18,170 --> 00:03:21,910
from the intestine
to the periphery and

49
00:03:21,910 --> 00:03:27,010
liver which are used
in energy and storage.

50
00:03:27,790 --> 00:03:34,110
LDL and LDL are involved
in the transport

51
00:03:34,110 --> 00:03:39,210
of hepatic lipids to
the periphery. In other

52
00:03:39,210 --> 00:03:42,190
words, from the liver
to the periphery.

53
00:03:42,550 --> 00:03:46,150
The HDL is involved
in transport of

54
00:03:46,150 --> 00:03:52,670
excess VLDL, IDL, and
LDL from the periphery

55
00:03:52,670 --> 00:03:55,230
back to the liver
for processing.

56
00:03:57,330 --> 00:04:02,050
In the exogenous
pathway, chylomicrons

57
00:04:02,050 --> 00:04:05,870
transport dietary fat
from the intestine to

58
00:04:05,870 --> 00:04:09,550
tissues that require
fatty acids for energy

59
00:04:09,550 --> 00:04:12,850
and storage and
cholesterol to the liver.

60
00:04:12,850 --> 00:04:15,750
In the endogenous pathway,

61
00:04:15,970 --> 00:04:19,070
hepatic lipids are
transported from

62
00:04:19,070 --> 00:04:22,250
the liver to the
periphery to provide

63
00:04:22,250 --> 00:04:25,150
a source of energy
during fasting.

64
00:04:27,110 --> 00:04:32,250
HDL pathway transports
excess cholesterol from the

65
00:04:32,250 --> 00:04:36,090
periphery back to the
liver for excretion in the

66
00:04:36,090 --> 00:04:40,410
bile. Only hepatocytes
and enterocytes can

67
00:04:40,410 --> 00:04:44,750
effectively excrete cholesterol
from the body. In the

68
00:04:44,750 --> 00:04:49,250
liver, cholesterol is
secreted into the bile either

69
00:04:49,250 --> 00:04:53,930
directly or after
conversion to bile acids and

70
00:04:53,930 --> 00:04:58,510
pterocytes excrete cholesterol
into the gut lumen.

71
00:05:01,560 --> 00:05:05,080
We will now move
on to dyslipidemia

72
00:05:05,410 --> 00:05:07,730
and its role in disease.

73
00:05:09,250 --> 00:05:13,310
The clinical significance
for dyslipidemia

74
00:05:13,310 --> 00:05:15,650
is that they can contribute to

75
00:05:15,650 --> 00:05:18,220
the development of
antherosclerosis.

76
00:05:18,950 --> 00:05:24,490
Antherosclerosis is a
known factor in coronary

77
00:05:24,490 --> 00:05:27,510
artery disease, peripheral
vascular disease,

78
00:05:27,550 --> 00:05:31,490
and cerebrovascular
accidents. All of these

79
00:05:31,490 --> 00:05:34,730
can cause significant
problems for the patients

80
00:05:34,730 --> 00:05:37,990
who have them, including
leading to death.

81
00:05:38,310 --> 00:05:43,410
Severe hyper
triglyceridemia may lead to

82
00:05:43,410 --> 00:05:48,570
acute pancreatitis.
The clinical element in

83
00:05:48,570 --> 00:05:53,130
this is non-alcoholic
fatty liver disease.

84
00:05:56,720 --> 00:06:01,130
Anthrosclerosis is a
very common disease that

85
00:06:01,130 --> 00:06:05,030
affects the arteries
and is caused by buildup

86
00:06:05,030 --> 00:06:08,730
of cholesterol plaques.
These plaques are

87
00:06:08,730 --> 00:06:13,930
formed by macrophages
and LDL being accumulated

88
00:06:13,930 --> 00:06:18,350
and forming a
complex antheromas.

89
00:06:18,830 --> 00:06:21,630
Complications of
these formations

90
00:06:21,630 --> 00:06:26,090
is ischemia, thrombosformation,

91
00:06:26,410 --> 00:06:30,270
emboli, and aneurysms
in the areas affected.

92
00:06:30,890 --> 00:06:35,870
Symptoms for the
patients include angina,

93
00:06:36,270 --> 00:06:37,470
claudication,

94
00:06:37,850 --> 00:06:40,670
and often asymptomatic.

95
00:06:42,570 --> 00:06:47,290
Atheromas tend to form
in areas of the arteries

96
00:06:47,290 --> 00:06:50,730
that are exposed to
increased shear stress,

97
00:06:50,730 --> 00:06:55,090
such as bifurcations and
bending points leading

98
00:06:55,090 --> 00:06:59,050
to the exposure of the
subendothelial tissue.

99
00:06:59,580 --> 00:07:04,830
Platelet aggregates or
microthrombi form due to

100
00:07:04,830 --> 00:07:09,610
platelet adherence to the
exposed subendothelial tissue.

101
00:07:09,610 --> 00:07:13,510
These events initiate a
cascade that eventually

102
00:07:13,510 --> 00:07:17,490
leads to the formation
of antheromas.

103
00:07:21,230 --> 00:07:26,390
Risk factors for developing
antherosclerosis include

104
00:07:26,390 --> 00:07:31,190
age, which progressive
with each decade of life.

105
00:07:31,430 --> 00:07:35,390
Male gender is more affected
than the female gender.

106
00:07:35,830 --> 00:07:38,850
Family history of a patient

107
00:07:38,850 --> 00:07:41,670
that includes hypertension,

108
00:07:41,890 --> 00:07:42,890
diabetes,

109
00:07:43,370 --> 00:07:47,330
or familial
hypercholesterolemia

110
00:07:47,330 --> 00:07:50,210
increases this patient's risk.

111
00:07:50,770 --> 00:07:55,930
Cigarette smoking of the
affected patient would also

112
00:07:55,930 --> 00:07:58,750
increase the risk. This
is a modifiable risk

113
00:07:58,750 --> 00:08:04,530
factor. Patients who stopped
smoking would improve and

114
00:08:04,530 --> 00:08:09,510
decrease the risk of
developing antherosclerosis.

115
00:08:09,810 --> 00:08:13,910
The presence in the
patient of hypertension,

116
00:08:13,910 --> 00:08:17,730
whether it is
systolic or diastolic,

117
00:08:18,530 --> 00:08:24,370
Hyperlipidemia, which is
when primarily the LDL

118
00:08:24,370 --> 00:08:29,950
is elevated and also the
low HDL, which the low

119
00:08:29,950 --> 00:08:34,150
HDL is an independent
risk factor on its own.

120
00:08:34,610 --> 00:08:39,090
Presence of diabetes
or metabolic syndrome.

121
00:08:41,850 --> 00:08:46,090
Metabolic syndrome
is a group of risk

122
00:08:46,090 --> 00:08:50,030
factors and it's
defined by three or more

123
00:08:50,030 --> 00:08:52,700
of the following
five abnormalities.

124
00:08:53,130 --> 00:08:58,470
The presence of fasting
blood glucose of greater

125
00:08:58,470 --> 00:09:05,050
than or equal to 100
milligrams per deciliter, a

126
00:09:05,050 --> 00:09:11,170
blood pressure of at least
130 over 85 milligrams,

127
00:09:12,410 --> 00:09:17,090
triglycerides that are
greater or equal to 150

128
00:09:17,090 --> 00:09:22,150
milligrams per deciliter,
HDL of a level of less than

129
00:09:22,150 --> 00:09:26,950
40 milligrams per deciliter
in men or less than 50

130
00:09:26,950 --> 00:09:31,050
milligrams per deciliter
in women, and a waist

131
00:09:31,050 --> 00:09:37,870
circumference of 40 inches
in men or 35 inches in women.

132
00:09:40,470 --> 00:09:43,590
We will now move on to discuss

133
00:09:43,590 --> 00:09:46,730
the ideology of dyslipidemia.

134
00:09:48,470 --> 00:09:54,390
Primary causes of
dyspidemia generally are

135
00:09:54,390 --> 00:09:59,930
single or multiple gene
mutations which result

136
00:09:59,930 --> 00:10:04,810
in either overproduction
or defective clearance

137
00:10:04,810 --> 00:10:11,470
of triglycerides and
LDL cholesterol, or

138
00:10:11,470 --> 00:10:16,910
underproduction or
excessive clearance of HDL.

139
00:10:21,750 --> 00:10:25,970
Familial hypercholesterolemia
is a primary cause

140
00:10:25,970 --> 00:10:31,910
of dyslipidemia. It is
resulted due to a gene defect

141
00:10:31,910 --> 00:10:37,330
in the LDL receptor,
which causes diminished

142
00:10:37,330 --> 00:10:43,290
clearance of LDL. The
inheritance is codominant,

143
00:10:43,290 --> 00:10:48,170
customarily, or complex with
multiple gene involvement.

144
00:10:48,310 --> 00:10:52,730
The prevalence for
heterozygotes is 1 in

145
00:10:52,730 --> 00:11:00,230
200 and homozygotes
in 1 in every 250,000

146
00:11:00,230 --> 00:11:05,970
to 1 in every 1 million.
In heterozygotes,

147
00:11:06,130 --> 00:11:12,550
you generally see total
cholesterol between 250 and

148
00:11:12,550 --> 00:11:17,090
500 milligrams per
deciliter. There is premature

149
00:11:17,090 --> 00:11:22,810
coronary artery disease
between the ages of 30 to

150
00:11:22,810 --> 00:11:28,210
50, and in 5%, there is
a myocardial infarction

151
00:11:28,210 --> 00:11:34,950
before 60 years old. In
homozygotes, the triglycerides

152
00:11:34,950 --> 00:11:38,850
are greater than, excuse
me, the total cholesterol

153
00:11:38,850 --> 00:11:43,090
is greater than 500
milligrams per deciliter.

154
00:11:43,190 --> 00:11:47,810
And there is also
premature coronary artery

155
00:11:47,810 --> 00:11:51,330
disease, which occurs
before the age of 18.

156
00:11:52,970 --> 00:11:56,490
Familial combined
hyperlipidemia is another

157
00:11:56,490 --> 00:12:00,740
primary cause of
dysplipidemia. The genetic

158
00:12:00,740 --> 00:12:04,310
defect that is involved
in this case is unknown.

159
00:12:04,390 --> 00:12:07,090
It is possible that there are

160
00:12:07,090 --> 00:12:10,370
multiple defects involved.

161
00:12:10,370 --> 00:12:13,470
The inheritance is autosomal.

162
00:12:13,470 --> 00:12:20,550
The prevalence is between
1 in 150 to 1 in 100.

163
00:12:20,550 --> 00:12:25,930
There is premature coronary
artery disease, resulting

164
00:12:25,930 --> 00:12:31,970
in 15% of MIs in people
less than 50 years old.

165
00:12:32,970 --> 00:12:37,610
ApoB is disproportionately
elevated.

166
00:12:37,890 --> 00:12:40,670
Total cholesterol
customarily is

167
00:12:40,670 --> 00:12:44,690
between 250 and 500,
and triglycerides

168
00:12:44,690 --> 00:12:48,590
are customarily
between 250 and 750.

169
00:12:50,350 --> 00:12:54,470
Continuing with primary
causes of dyslipidemia,

170
00:12:54,470 --> 00:12:58,530
we have familial
hypertriglyceridemia.

171
00:12:59,470 --> 00:13:04,130
Its genetic defect is
unknown. It is likely

172
00:13:04,130 --> 00:13:08,510
that it is caused by
multiple genetic defects

173
00:13:08,510 --> 00:13:13,090
and mechanisms. It has
an autosomal dominant

174
00:13:13,090 --> 00:13:17,590
inheritance and a
prevalence of 1 out of 500.

175
00:13:17,590 --> 00:13:22,090
It customarily has no
symptoms or findings.

176
00:13:22,210 --> 00:13:26,250
There is absence of
secondary causes to make

177
00:13:26,250 --> 00:13:29,870
this diagnosis, and
the triglycerides are

178
00:13:29,870 --> 00:13:34,530
between 200 and 500
milligrams per deciliter.

179
00:13:35,610 --> 00:13:39,450
Another primary cause
of distalipinemia is

180
00:13:39,450 --> 00:13:45,210
familial defective
ApoB100. The genetic defect

181
00:13:45,210 --> 00:13:49,650
involved here is LDL
receptor binding region

182
00:13:49,650 --> 00:13:54,610
defect which causes
diminished clearance of LDL.

183
00:13:54,850 --> 00:13:58,010
Its inheritance is autosomal

184
00:13:58,010 --> 00:14:02,830
dominant. It is
prevalent in 1 in 700.

185
00:14:03,230 --> 00:14:08,370
It also has premature
coronary artery disease.

186
00:14:08,670 --> 00:14:11,510
There are symptomas and arches

187
00:14:11,510 --> 00:14:14,090
carnea present
on physical exam.

188
00:14:14,290 --> 00:14:18,510
The total cholesterol
is between 250

189
00:14:18,510 --> 00:14:21,810
and 500 milligrams
per deciliter.

190
00:14:23,190 --> 00:14:27,810
Familial HDL deficiency
is another primary cause

191
00:14:27,810 --> 00:14:36,790
of dyslipidemia. Its genetic
defect is ABCA1 gene,

192
00:14:37,430 --> 00:14:42,230
ATP binding cassette
transporter A1.

193
00:14:42,230 --> 00:14:46,610
The inheritance is autosomal
dominant, the prevalence

194
00:14:46,610 --> 00:14:51,510
is rare, and coronary
artery disease is also seen.

195
00:14:53,470 --> 00:14:58,610
Moving on now to secondary
causes of dyslipidemia.

196
00:14:59,100 --> 00:15:03,050
Secondary causes
contribute to many

197
00:15:03,050 --> 00:15:06,370
cases of dyslipidemias
in adults.

198
00:15:06,370 --> 00:15:11,390
The most important
secondary cause in

199
00:15:11,390 --> 00:15:14,350
developed countries
is a sedentary

200
00:15:14,350 --> 00:15:19,650
lifestyle. This is
totally modifiable.

201
00:15:20,330 --> 00:15:24,650
It includes an excessive
dietary intake of

202
00:15:24,650 --> 00:15:28,530
saturated fat,
cholesterol, and trans fat.

203
00:15:28,890 --> 00:15:34,710
modifying diet can
modify this important

204
00:15:34,710 --> 00:15:37,390
secondary cause
of dyslipidemia.

205
00:15:41,050 --> 00:15:45,630
Other common secondary causes
of dyslipidemia include

206
00:15:45,630 --> 00:15:50,910
endocrine disorders such
as diabetes mellitus,

207
00:15:50,910 --> 00:15:57,110
insulin resistance, Cushing's
disease and hypothyroidism.

208
00:15:57,110 --> 00:16:01,670
There are hepatic disorders
such as primary biliary

209
00:16:01,670 --> 00:16:06,270
cirrhosis and other
cholestatic liver diseases.

210
00:16:06,610 --> 00:16:11,170
Renal disorders,
which include chronic

211
00:16:11,170 --> 00:16:13,910
kidney disease and
nephrotic syndrome.

212
00:16:14,910 --> 00:16:18,330
Medications, there are
many culprits here,

213
00:16:18,330 --> 00:16:22,750
including thiazides,
beta blockers, retinoids,

214
00:16:22,750 --> 00:16:26,790
highly active
antiretroviral agents,

215
00:16:27,310 --> 00:16:30,290
estrogen and progestins, and

216
00:16:30,290 --> 00:16:35,850
corticosteroids. Other
causes include diet,

217
00:16:36,150 --> 00:16:37,410
obesity,

218
00:16:37,550 --> 00:16:39,670
and alcohol overuse.

219
00:16:40,790 --> 00:16:46,070
Diabetes mellitus is a
significant secondary cause

220
00:16:46,070 --> 00:16:52,050
of dyslipidemia. It has an
antherogenic combination

221
00:16:52,050 --> 00:17:00,350
of elevated triglycerides
and LDL and low HDL.

222
00:17:01,170 --> 00:17:06,680
This is exacerbated
by the precedence of

223
00:17:06,680 --> 00:17:11,010
obesity, sedentary
life or physical

224
00:17:11,010 --> 00:17:14,830
inactivity, and
increased caloric intake.

225
00:17:16,690 --> 00:17:20,490
Another secondary
cause of dyslipidemia

226
00:17:20,490 --> 00:17:24,870
is excessive hepatic
production of VLDL.

227
00:17:24,870 --> 00:17:28,890
This is characterized
by elevated fasting

228
00:17:28,890 --> 00:17:35,270
triglycerides, low HDL,
and variable levels of LDL.

229
00:17:35,730 --> 00:17:42,390
Common causes include high
carbohydrate diet, obesity

230
00:17:42,390 --> 00:17:48,290
and insulin resistance, in
which more free fatty acids

231
00:17:48,290 --> 00:17:52,730
are delivered from the
adipose tissue to the liver,

232
00:17:52,870 --> 00:17:57,990
and there is increased
insulin levels which

233
00:17:57,990 --> 00:18:01,450
promote increased
fatty acid synthesis.

234
00:18:01,910 --> 00:18:04,290
Also, as seen, neprotic

235
00:18:04,290 --> 00:18:07,590
syndrome and Cushing syndrome.

236
00:18:10,090 --> 00:18:12,990
Alcohol overuse is another

237
00:18:12,990 --> 00:18:15,350
secondary cause
of dyslipinemia.

238
00:18:15,530 --> 00:18:19,050
It causes excessive production

239
00:18:19,270 --> 00:18:23,090
of VLDL in the liver.

240
00:18:23,490 --> 00:18:28,570
It inhibits hepatic
oxidation of free fatty

241
00:18:28,570 --> 00:18:34,090
acids and promotes
hepatic triglyceride

242
00:18:34,090 --> 00:18:41,030
synthesis and that of
LDL VLDL secretion.

243
00:18:41,030 --> 00:18:46,070
It rises the plasma
levels of HDL.

244
00:18:46,380 --> 00:18:50,650
Consider this if you
see a combination

245
00:18:50,650 --> 00:18:55,930
of elevated
triglycerides and HDL.

246
00:18:58,990 --> 00:19:03,190
Continuing with secondary
causes of dyslipidemia,

247
00:19:03,550 --> 00:19:08,490
we have here impaired
lipolysis of triglyceride

248
00:19:08,490 --> 00:19:12,570
rich lipoproteins.
This occurs due to

249
00:19:12,570 --> 00:19:18,350
decreased LPL or
lipoprotein lipase activity.

250
00:19:18,550 --> 00:19:24,230
It is characterized by
elevated fasting triglycerides,

251
00:19:24,230 --> 00:19:32,310
low HDL, usually without
elevations of LDL or APLB.

252
00:19:32,590 --> 00:19:35,890
Common causes of this is

253
00:19:35,890 --> 00:19:38,810
obesity and insulin resistance.

254
00:19:40,270 --> 00:19:45,870
The impaired hepatic uptake
of lipoproteins containing

255
00:19:45,870 --> 00:19:50,230
APLB is another secondary
cause of dyslipidemia.

256
00:19:50,470 --> 00:19:54,510
Here you see
reduced LDL receptor

257
00:19:54,510 --> 00:20:00,230
activity, characterized
by elevated LDL.

258
00:20:00,570 --> 00:20:05,310
Common causes of this
is hypothyroidism,

259
00:20:05,310 --> 00:20:10,790
in which there is
increased IDL and mild

260
00:20:10,790 --> 00:20:15,490
elevation of
triglycerides, also seen in

261
00:20:15,490 --> 00:20:19,830
chronic kidney disease
in which there is mild

262
00:20:20,930 --> 00:20:24,510
hypertriglyceridemia
which is less

263
00:20:24,510 --> 00:20:27,770
than 300 milligrams
per deciliter.

264
00:20:30,850 --> 00:20:36,350
Reduced HDL levels is
considered another secondary

265
00:20:36,350 --> 00:20:42,070
cause of dyslipidemia. This
is caused by a combination

266
00:20:42,070 --> 00:20:47,010
of genetic prediposition
and secondary factors.

267
00:20:47,210 --> 00:20:51,470
This is an independent
predictor for

268
00:20:51,470 --> 00:20:55,850
increased cardiovascular
risk all by itself.

269
00:20:56,410 --> 00:21:02,290
HDL metabolism is
influenced by triglyceride

270
00:21:02,290 --> 00:21:06,430
-rich lipoproteins,
insulin resistance,

271
00:21:06,590 --> 00:21:12,610
and inflammation. Secondary
causes of low levels

272
00:21:12,610 --> 00:21:17,310
of HDL cholesterol
include cigarette smoking,

273
00:21:17,590 --> 00:21:19,430
anabolic steroids,

274
00:21:19,630 --> 00:21:22,970
HIV infection, and
neurotic syndrome.

275
00:21:24,790 --> 00:21:30,870
Certain liver disorders
and drugs are also

276
00:21:30,870 --> 00:21:35,110
within the secondary
causes of dyslipidemia.

277
00:21:35,110 --> 00:21:37,510
For the liver
disorders, we have

278
00:21:37,510 --> 00:21:41,430
hepatitis, which can be
caused by infections,

279
00:21:41,650 --> 00:21:45,370
drugs, or alcohol,
which are associated

280
00:21:45,370 --> 00:21:49,270
with increased
VLDL synthesis and

281
00:21:49,270 --> 00:21:52,420
mild to moderate
hypertriglycyremia.

282
00:21:53,650 --> 00:21:59,250
Cholestasis is associated
with hypercholesterolemia,

283
00:21:59,250 --> 00:22:04,010
which can be severe.
Drugs that are

284
00:22:04,010 --> 00:22:08,530
included in this group
are beta blockers, which

285
00:22:08,530 --> 00:22:15,310
reduce HDL and you see
also elevated VLDL.

286
00:22:15,510 --> 00:22:22,450
With thiazides you will see
an elevated LDL and with

287
00:22:22,450 --> 00:22:29,570
estrogens you will see
elevated HDL, elevated VLDL,

288
00:22:29,570 --> 00:22:33,930
and triglycerides. These
are all common medications,

289
00:22:33,930 --> 00:22:38,650
so make sure that you are
aware of these effects.

290
00:22:39,930 --> 00:22:43,890
Our next topic is signs and

291
00:22:43,890 --> 00:22:47,470
symptoms related
to dyslipidemia.

292
00:22:49,850 --> 00:22:53,950
Dyslipidemia in
itself is usually

293
00:22:53,950 --> 00:22:59,330
asymptomatic. No symptoms
are present. However,

294
00:22:59,570 --> 00:23:04,270
it leads to symptomatic
vascular disease,

295
00:23:04,370 --> 00:23:08,670
which includes coronary
artery disease, stroke,

296
00:23:08,830 --> 00:23:11,410
peripheral arterial disease.

297
00:23:11,990 --> 00:23:17,330
Note that an extremely
high triglyceride levels

298
00:23:17,330 --> 00:23:23,510
can give a lactase
appearance to blood plasma.

299
00:23:25,290 --> 00:23:30,410
Symptoms when this
is present are

300
00:23:30,410 --> 00:23:34,450
paresthesias, dyspnea,
and confusion.

301
00:23:34,850 --> 00:23:39,630
You can see here a
tube that of someone

302
00:23:39,630 --> 00:23:43,610
that has very high
levels of triglycerides.

303
00:23:51,710 --> 00:23:55,990
Take note that high
levels of triglycerides,

304
00:23:55,990 --> 00:23:59,490
meaning greater than
1,000 milligrams

305
00:23:59,490 --> 00:24:04,550
per deciliter can cause
acute pancreatitis.

306
00:24:04,770 --> 00:24:06,630
Take note again,

307
00:24:06,630 --> 00:24:10,850
severe elevations of
triglycerides can present

308
00:24:10,850 --> 00:24:15,230
with eruptive symptoms
over the trunk,

309
00:24:15,230 --> 00:24:20,210
back, elbow, buttocks,
knees, hands, and feet.

310
00:24:22,290 --> 00:24:27,850
Severe hypertriglycerinia
greater than 2,000 milligrams

311
00:24:27,850 --> 00:24:33,970
per deciliter can present
with lipemia retinalis.

312
00:24:37,450 --> 00:24:44,170
High levels of LDL can
present with arcus cornea

313
00:24:44,170 --> 00:24:50,170
and tendinosis as depicted
here in this picture.

314
00:24:52,170 --> 00:24:57,890
Physical exam findings for
hypercholesterolemia include

315
00:24:57,890 --> 00:25:03,270
tendinosis xanthomas.
These begins with tendon

316
00:25:03,270 --> 00:25:09,810
thickening at the lateral
border. Occur mainly in the

317
00:25:09,810 --> 00:25:14,250
extensor tendons of the hands,
feet, elbows, and knees.

318
00:25:15,310 --> 00:25:20,630
You can can also see
tuberous xanthomas. These are

319
00:25:20,630 --> 00:25:25,590
firm, painless yellow or red
nodules which are usually

320
00:25:25,590 --> 00:25:30,630
found over extensor aspects
of the limbs and buttocks.

321
00:25:35,640 --> 00:25:39,320
Other physical exam findings
for hypercholesterolemia

322
00:25:39,340 --> 00:25:43,740
includes Arcus cornea
which results from

323
00:25:43,740 --> 00:25:47,640
cholesterol infiltration
of the corneal rim.

324
00:25:49,260 --> 00:25:54,560
Xanthelesmas are yellow
cholesterol plaques that occur

325
00:25:54,560 --> 00:25:59,320
most commonly near the inner
canthus, usually of the

326
00:25:59,320 --> 00:26:05,440
upper eyelid. Both of these
are very common findings.

327
00:26:06,080 --> 00:26:10,550
Physical exam findings
for hypertriglycyremia

328
00:26:10,580 --> 00:26:14,520
includes eruptive
than xanthomas.

329
00:26:14,720 --> 00:26:18,920
These are painless
yellow papules

330
00:26:18,920 --> 00:26:22,400
that present as
groups of lesions

331
00:26:22,810 --> 00:26:24,540
on the torso,

332
00:26:24,780 --> 00:26:28,520
elbows, chest, and buttocks.

333
00:26:30,490 --> 00:26:33,780
Our next topic in
this presentation

334
00:26:33,780 --> 00:26:38,160
includes diagnosis
of dyslipidemia.

335
00:26:40,200 --> 00:26:45,660
Clinical manifestations
of dyslipidemia may

336
00:26:45,660 --> 00:26:49,140
present as one or
more of the following.

337
00:26:49,420 --> 00:26:53,180
Elevated total
plasma cholesterol,

338
00:26:53,220 --> 00:26:57,540
elevated low
-density lipoprotein,

339
00:26:57,560 --> 00:27:00,780
elevated triglycerides, and

340
00:27:00,780 --> 00:27:04,240
decreased high
-density lipoprotein.

341
00:27:05,760 --> 00:27:10,920
The diagnosis for
dyslipidemia is

342
00:27:10,920 --> 00:27:14,480
done by measuring serum lipids.

343
00:27:14,760 --> 00:27:18,160
The serum lipid
profile includes

344
00:27:18,160 --> 00:27:22,180
total cholesterol,
triglycerides,

345
00:27:22,540 --> 00:27:24,220
HDL cholesterol,

346
00:27:24,380 --> 00:27:29,680
and calculated LDL cholesterol
and VLDL cholesterol.

347
00:27:29,770 --> 00:27:32,680
The formula is
total cholesterol

348
00:27:32,680 --> 00:27:38,440
equals VLDL plus LDL plus HDL.

349
00:27:41,550 --> 00:27:45,140
Note that in a
serum lipid profile,

350
00:27:45,140 --> 00:27:48,540
total cholesterol,
triglycerides, and

351
00:27:48,540 --> 00:27:52,700
HDL cholesterol are
measured directly.

352
00:27:53,020 --> 00:27:58,000
Total cholesterol
values can vary by 10%

353
00:27:58,000 --> 00:28:03,160
and triglycerides by
up to 25% day to day,

354
00:28:03,200 --> 00:28:06,820
even in the absence
of a disorder. So it's

355
00:28:06,820 --> 00:28:09,580
normal that you would
see this variation.

356
00:28:10,080 --> 00:28:13,740
Patients should have
all lipids measured

357
00:28:13,740 --> 00:28:17,980
while fasting,
usually for 12 hours,

358
00:28:17,980 --> 00:28:21,500
for maximum accuracy
and consistency.

359
00:28:21,640 --> 00:28:25,660
Again, they should
have the levels done

360
00:28:25,660 --> 00:28:29,720
while fasting for
at least 12 hours.

361
00:28:30,120 --> 00:28:34,900
Testing should be postponed
until after resolution of

362
00:28:34,900 --> 00:28:40,080
acute illness. This is
because triglycerides and

363
00:28:40,080 --> 00:28:45,300
lipoprotein levels increase
and cholesterol levels decrease

364
00:28:45,300 --> 00:28:50,580
when there is the presence
of an inflammatory state.

365
00:28:52,680 --> 00:28:56,800
The LDL cholesterol
is customarily

366
00:28:56,800 --> 00:29:02,440
calculated in a
serum lipid profile.

367
00:29:02,580 --> 00:29:07,880
This calculation the LDL
equals the total cholesterol

368
00:29:07,880 --> 00:29:14,760
minus the HDL plus the
triglycerides divided by five.

369
00:29:14,760 --> 00:29:21,140
This calculation is valid
only when triglycerides are

370
00:29:21,140 --> 00:29:25,640
less than 400 milligrams
per deciliters and patients

371
00:29:25,640 --> 00:29:30,720
are fasting because eating
increases triglycerides.

372
00:29:31,380 --> 00:29:36,320
You can request a
direct LDL measurement

373
00:29:36,320 --> 00:29:38,940
when the triglycerides
are greater

374
00:29:38,940 --> 00:29:41,960
than 400 milligrams
per deciliter.

375
00:29:42,420 --> 00:29:48,120
Direct LDL measurements
are not routinely necessary

376
00:29:48,120 --> 00:29:55,860
because the LDL calculated
one is approximately

377
00:29:55,860 --> 00:30:02,240
the same when the triglycerides
are less than 400.

378
00:30:02,240 --> 00:30:05,260
So they're close to
being very accurate.

379
00:30:07,880 --> 00:30:13,820
Screening for dyslipidemia.
Universal screening

380
00:30:14,210 --> 00:30:22,280
use a fasting lipid profile
should be done in once

381
00:30:22,280 --> 00:30:28,340
for all children between
the age of 9 and 11 or at

382
00:30:28,340 --> 00:30:33,460
2 if children have a
family history of severe

383
00:30:33,460 --> 00:30:38,060
hyperlipidemia or premature
coronary artery disease.

384
00:30:38,300 --> 00:30:42,700
Adults are screened at age 20

385
00:30:42,700 --> 00:30:45,540
and every five
years thereafter.

386
00:30:46,060 --> 00:30:48,740
Assessment for cardiovascular

387
00:30:48,740 --> 00:30:52,560
risk factors should accompany
the lipid measurements.

388
00:30:52,940 --> 00:30:56,060
A definite age to discontinue

389
00:30:56,060 --> 00:30:58,700
screening has not
been determined.

390
00:31:00,370 --> 00:31:04,520
It should be noted that
screening in certain circumstance

391
00:31:04,520 --> 00:31:09,400
can be done more frequently
than is noted here.

392
00:31:12,020 --> 00:31:15,840
Screening for secondary
causes of dyslipidemia

393
00:31:15,840 --> 00:31:19,640
should be considered
with newly diagnosed

394
00:31:19,710 --> 00:31:24,000
dyslipidemia and or
when a component of the

395
00:31:24,000 --> 00:31:28,900
lipid profile has changed
for the worth without

396
00:31:28,900 --> 00:31:33,900
an explanation. Consider
fasting glucose,

397
00:31:34,020 --> 00:31:35,800
liver enzymes,

398
00:31:36,140 --> 00:31:38,500
creatinine, thyroid stimulating

399
00:31:38,500 --> 00:31:41,480
hormone, and urinary protein.

400
00:31:41,480 --> 00:31:47,680
Once secondary causes ruled
out, attempt to determine

401
00:31:47,680 --> 00:31:52,340
if there are primary
causes of dyslipidemia.

402
00:31:55,620 --> 00:31:59,580
For the diagnosis
of primary cause of

403
00:31:59,580 --> 00:32:04,000
a dyslipidemia in
chylomicronemia, you

404
00:32:04,000 --> 00:32:07,280
would do this with
the fasting plasma.

405
00:32:07,600 --> 00:32:12,940
And if there is the presence
of a triglyceride level

406
00:32:12,940 --> 00:32:17,220
of greater than a thousand
milligrams per deciliter, you

407
00:32:17,220 --> 00:32:23,100
can consider familial
chylomicronemia syndrome in

408
00:32:23,100 --> 00:32:27,640
which the cholesterol to
triglyceride ratio is greater

409
00:32:27,640 --> 00:32:33,880
than 10 and these individuals
would be at risk for acute

410
00:32:33,880 --> 00:32:39,320
pancreatitis as noted
previously. For familial

411
00:32:39,320 --> 00:32:45,920
hypercholesterolemia, LDL levels
are elevated in the absence

412
00:32:45,920 --> 00:32:52,960
of hypertriglycidemia. This
is a clinical diagnosis.

413
00:32:54,540 --> 00:33:00,780
Combined hyperlipidemia is
another primary cause of

414
00:33:00,780 --> 00:33:07,240
dyslipidemia. It It is
diagnosed by obtaining an

415
00:33:07,240 --> 00:33:15,380
elevation of triglycerides,
VLDL and LDL in serum lipids.

416
00:33:15,950 --> 00:33:20,900
You would determine the
VLDL to triglyceride ratio

417
00:33:20,900 --> 00:33:26,940
in plasma or direct
LDL to determine if the

418
00:33:26,940 --> 00:33:32,680
hyperlipidemia is due to
accumulation of lipoprotein

419
00:33:32,680 --> 00:33:40,980
revenants, that is in familial
dysbeta-lipoproteinemia,

420
00:33:40,980 --> 00:33:46,940
or an increase in both
LDL and VLDL is present.

421
00:33:47,280 --> 00:33:53,600
The measurement of APOB
levels can help identify

422
00:33:53,600 --> 00:33:58,620
patients with familial
combined hyperlipidemia.

423
00:34:01,710 --> 00:34:05,960
We will now move on to
the American College of

424
00:34:05,960 --> 00:34:09,180
Cardiology and American
Heart Association Task

425
00:34:09,180 --> 00:34:13,780
Force Clinical Practice
Guidelines from 2026.

426
00:34:23,120 --> 00:34:28,000
According to the AHCC
and AHA guidelines of

427
00:34:28,000 --> 00:34:31,960
2026, the main indication
for treatment of

428
00:34:31,960 --> 00:34:37,500
dyslipidemia is the
prevention of ASCVD or

429
00:34:37,500 --> 00:34:40,960
antherosclerotic cardiovascular
disease, including

430
00:34:40,960 --> 00:34:43,640
acute coronary syndrome,
stroke, transient

431
00:34:43,640 --> 00:34:47,360
ischemic attack, and
peripheral vascular disease.

432
00:34:49,260 --> 00:34:54,640
The current guidelines
recommend treating

433
00:34:54,640 --> 00:34:59,880
dyslipidemia earlier to
reduce the lifelong risk of

434
00:34:59,880 --> 00:35:04,820
prolonged exposure to
anthrogenic lipoprotein.

435
00:35:05,220 --> 00:35:10,130
These treatment guidelines
include lifestyle

436
00:35:10,130 --> 00:35:13,920
optimization that should
start in youth, including

437
00:35:13,920 --> 00:35:18,120
childhood. Consider
pharmacotherapy in youth with

438
00:35:18,120 --> 00:35:22,000
familial hypercholesterolemia
and in young adults

439
00:35:22,000 --> 00:35:27,000
with an LDC of greater
than 160 milligrams per

440
00:35:27,000 --> 00:35:32,160
deciliter or family
history of premature ASCVD.

441
00:35:32,160 --> 00:35:38,900
They also recommend to
use the AHA Prevent Risk

442
00:35:38,900 --> 00:35:43,740
Calculator to determine the
10-year risk of ASCVD. The

443
00:35:48,820 --> 00:35:54,580
primary prevention of
ASCVD with LDL medication

444
00:35:54,580 --> 00:35:59,320
therapy in adults should
begin with a prevent

445
00:35:59,320 --> 00:36:07,040
ASCVD risk estimate of
3-2 less than 5% and

446
00:36:07,040 --> 00:36:13,220
should be considered for
those having a 5%-2 less

447
00:36:13,220 --> 00:36:20,820
than 10% risk. Testing
for apolopoprotein B can

448
00:36:20,820 --> 00:36:23,160
improve risk assessment,
particularly in

449
00:36:23,160 --> 00:36:26,640
individuals with elevated
triglycerides or diabetes.

450
00:36:27,200 --> 00:36:31,560
Lipoprotein A should be
assessed at least once

451
00:36:31,560 --> 00:36:35,820
to determine individuals
at risk for ASCVD.

452
00:36:37,880 --> 00:36:43,600
A coronary artery calcium
scoring can be beneficial

453
00:36:43,600 --> 00:36:48,580
in men at least 40 years
old and women at 45 year

454
00:36:48,580 --> 00:36:54,940
old, which can improve the
assessment and guide LDL-C

455
00:36:54,940 --> 00:37:03,720
and non-HDLC goals. ldl
lowering therapy is recommended

456
00:37:03,720 --> 00:37:07,620
as primary prevention
in adults between 40 and

457
00:37:07,620 --> 00:37:12,560
75 years old with diabetes
chronic kidney disease

458
00:37:12,560 --> 00:37:19,560
stage 3 or 4 or hiv in
secondary prevention a goal of

459
00:37:19,560 --> 00:37:25,920
LDL-C less than 55 milligrams
per deciliter and non

460
00:37:25,920 --> 00:37:30,960
-HDL-C less than 85
milligrams per deciliter is

461
00:37:30,960 --> 00:37:37,140
recommended for those at very
high risk of ASCVD events.

462
00:37:39,120 --> 00:37:41,840
In secondary prevention,

463
00:37:42,080 --> 00:37:46,780
a goal of LDL-C of less
than 55 milligrams per

464
00:37:46,780 --> 00:37:51,240
deciliter and non
-HDL-C of less than 85

465
00:37:51,240 --> 00:37:55,460
milligrams per deciliter
is recommended for those

466
00:37:55,460 --> 00:38:00,480
individuals at very high
risk of ASCVD events.

467
00:38:01,580 --> 00:38:06,820
Patients with persistently
elevated triglycerides

468
00:38:06,820 --> 00:38:10,660
statin therapy still
remains the foundation

469
00:38:10,660 --> 00:38:15,580
pharmacotherapy along with
lifestyle intervention to reduce

470
00:38:15,580 --> 00:38:20,060
ASCVD risk. In individuals
with triglyceride levels

471
00:38:20,060 --> 00:38:23,840
of greater than 1,000
milligrams per deciliter,

472
00:38:23,960 --> 00:38:26,260
treatment with triglyceride

473
00:38:26,260 --> 00:38:28,740
lowering therapies
helps prevent

474
00:38:33,080 --> 00:38:37,340
The American Heart
Association and the American

475
00:38:37,340 --> 00:38:41,940
College of Cardiology
recommends treatment with a

476
00:38:41,940 --> 00:38:47,000
statin for four specific
group of patients in the

477
00:38:47,000 --> 00:38:51,460
presence of clinical
anthrosclerotic cardiovascular

478
00:38:51,460 --> 00:38:57,940
disease. When the LDL LDL
cholesterol is greater

479
00:38:57,940 --> 00:39:03,380
than or equal to 190
milligrams per deciliter.

480
00:39:03,780 --> 00:39:09,800
In patients ages 40 to
75 with diabetes and

481
00:39:09,800 --> 00:39:16,220
LDL cholesterol between
70 to 189 milligrams

482
00:39:16,220 --> 00:39:19,460
per deciliter. Here,
the treatment goal

483
00:39:19,460 --> 00:39:24,320
is less than 70
milligrams per deciliter.

484
00:39:24,420 --> 00:39:32,860
Age 40 to 75 with an LDL
cholesterol between 70 and 189

485
00:39:32,860 --> 00:39:38,060
milligrams per deciliter
and an estimated 10-year

486
00:39:38,060 --> 00:39:47,900
antherosclerotic cardiovascular
disease of 7.5% or more.

487
00:39:53,740 --> 00:39:57,700
The risk of antherosclerotic
cardiovascular

488
00:39:57,700 --> 00:40:02,660
disease is estimating
using a risk

489
00:40:02,660 --> 00:40:05,940
calculator that
takes into account.

490
00:40:06,260 --> 00:40:10,040
and this risk calculator is
from the American College

491
00:40:10,040 --> 00:40:13,160
of Cardiology and the
American Heart Association.

492
00:40:13,680 --> 00:40:19,540
It includes the sex
of the patient, age,

493
00:40:19,560 --> 00:40:26,100
race, total cholesterol
and HDL cholesterol,

494
00:40:26,460 --> 00:40:29,980
the systolic and
diastolic blood pressure,

495
00:40:30,340 --> 00:40:35,280
use of antihypertensives
or statins,

496
00:40:35,540 --> 00:40:38,480
presence or absence
of diabetes,

497
00:40:38,640 --> 00:40:41,320
and smoker status.

498
00:40:42,080 --> 00:40:45,400
All of these are
